{"work_id":"raja-rani","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source_scene_number":null,"scene_status":"verified","unit_count":11,"units":[{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u001","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d001","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராசா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":61,"printed_page":60}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Rani, a widow? No—no, never! Rani is not a widow. Don't cast a stain on that diamond moon and throw dust over my life, Babu!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u002","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d002","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"பாபு","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Hmm... Rani, a jasmine no one has smelled—a rose untouched by hand! You alone are her Raja! My friend, I have no ruinous wish to pour out colourful, magical words like that and turn your golden future into a poisonous pool. I say this before the gods themselves: don't mistake tongues of fire for the red petals of a honeyed flower! Hmm... and don't think, 'What is this fellow doing, merely repeating lines he spoke in some play?' These are truths springing forth from the feeling of friendship!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u003","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d003","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராஜா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Enough, Babu, enough! Don't destroy the sweet memories of ours that are wandering in the breeze, Babu!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u004","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d004","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"பாபு","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"What do I care? Go however you like! I'm telling you she's a widow—a crushed flower. If my voice doesn't reach the black bee's ear, what can I do about it?","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u005","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d005","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராசா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Babu! Even if Rani is a widow, what of it? The gold ornament and flower garland may be gone, but has the widow's garb ever swallowed my beloved's youth—her heart?","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u006","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d006","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"பாபு","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Then what does your heart say?","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u007","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d007","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராஜா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"It agrees to remarriage, Babu! Yes, it agrees to remarriage!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u008","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d008","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"பாபு","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Ah! Besh, besh! I admire your resolve, my friend. But do you know what angers me about Rani? She has hidden from you all these days that she is a widow! Then what a great trickster she must be!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u009","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d009","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராசா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Yes—but Babu, only if she really were a widow could she have told me beforehand!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u010","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d010","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"பாபு","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Exactly! Yours is the story of the vetala climbing the murungai tree all over again. Hmm, Raja—why should I get into needless trouble? Ask that flattering Rani yourself. Then you'll see all the daytime disguises of that 'chaste woman'!","mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The proverbial `வேதாளம் ... முருக்க மரம்` image is retained rather than replaced with a different English proverb."]}},{"id":"raja-rani-en-s044-u011","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","target_language":"en","scene_id":"raja-rani-s044","archival_scene_ordinal":44,"source":{"source_path":"works/raja-rani/dialogues/records/scene-044.json","canonical_scene_path":"works/raja-rani/scenes/scene-044.md","source_record_id":"raja-rani-s044-d011","source_occurrence_id":null,"source_locator":null,"speaker_label":"ராஜா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61},{"pdf_page":63,"printed_page":62}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Babu, speak carefully! If you want the friendship that has arisen again between you and me not to die, don't keep plucking at such strings of discord!","english_page_segments":[{"pdf_page":62,"printed_page":61,"english_text":"Babu, speak carefully! If you want the friendship that has arisen again between you and me not to die—"},{"pdf_page":63,"printed_page":62,"english_text":"then don't keep plucking at such strings of discord!"}],"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["One source utterance crosses PDF 62→63 and remains one translation unit."]}}]}